    "narrative": "With today being October 4th, the Zurich Zebras are operating with a significantly thinned roster as several core pieces are off-duty. **Christian Yelich** serves as our primary anchor today against M. King, clocking in with a solid 66.28 efficiency score. While his base projection is moderate, the 13% boost from the platoon advantage against a right-handed arm and his recent high-contact output make him an essential start despite a slight drag from King\u2019s moderate xERA. Because our speed-focused assets like **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Caleb Durbin** are currently sidelined by the schedule, we are forced to lean on **Christian Yelich** to maintain our efficiency baseline, as the lack of stolen base threats on the active roster today makes it difficult to manufacture runs in the typical Zebras style.\n\nThe bench decision process today was largely moot due to the sheer number of off-days for key contributors like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Trea Turner**. **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** remain our most intriguing power-profile holds, but without favorable park factors or matchup data available for inactive players, they offer zero contribution to today\u2019s categories. We are proceeding with a restricted lineup, meaning the focus shifts entirely to managing the limited upside of **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Hector Rodriguez**. Investors should note that the absence of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Caleb Durbin** significantly lowers our projected stolen base ceiling; if **Gary Sanchez** or **Josh Smith** fail to provide immediate RBI production, the team\u2019s aggregate 5x5 output will be heavily suppressed. We are effectively in a \"hold pattern\" today, waiting for the return of our speed-specialist core, including **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**, to restore our tactical edge on the basepaths.",
